From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rog5 <rog5@localhost>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 20:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wayland/dma-buf: Keep the client's stride (drop the
 128-byte "correction")

The mobile-shell fork overwrote plane 0's stride of every linux-dmabuf
buffer with ALIGN(width * 4, 128), a device-specific hack. On the ROG
Phone 5 (Adreno 660, freedreno/Turnip) clients allocate wider strides
(e.g. 8704 for a 2144-px row): the forced 8576 made the EGL import fail,
Xwayland got a protocol error and was killed ("failed to import supplied
dmabufs: EGL failed to allocate resources"), and the shell stopped
answering for 45 s while Steam started. It is also wrong for any format
that is not 32 bpp. Upstream mutter trusts the client's stride.
---
 src/wayland/meta-wayland-dma-buf.c | 8 --------
 1 file changed, 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/wayland/meta-wayland-dma-buf.c b/src/wayland/meta-wayland-dma-buf.c
--- a/src/wayland/meta-wayland-dma-buf.c
+++ b/src/wayland/meta-wayland-dma-buf.c
@@ -1181,7 +1181,6 @@
   MetaWaylandBuffer *buffer;
   struct wl_resource *buffer_resource;
   GError *error = NULL;
-  int corrected_stride;
 
   dma_buf = wl_resource_get_user_data (params_resource);
   if (!dma_buf)
@@ -1222,13 +1221,6 @@
   dma_buf->drm_format = drm_format;
   dma_buf->is_y_inverted = !(flags & ZWP_LINUX_BUFFER_PARAMS_V1_FLAGS_Y_INVERT);
 
-  corrected_stride = (int) (128.f * (ceilf ((float) (dma_buf->width * 4) / 128.f)));
-  if (dma_buf->strides[0] != corrected_stride)
-    {
-      g_warning("DMABuf stride of %d corrected to %d", dma_buf->strides[0], corrected_stride);
-      dma_buf->strides[0] = corrected_stride;
-    }
-
   if (flags & ~ZWP_LINUX_BUFFER_PARAMS_V1_FLAGS_Y_INVERT)
     {
       wl_resource_post_error (params_resource,
-- 
2.50.0
